note Translation of Glob::required_ext from ripgrep (crates/globset/src/glob.rs).

note UNCLEAR: the doc has no Char type. Rust's char is assumed to be `Char`, with literals written as one-character text.
note Token as defined in globset: every variant is listed because the match below must handle each one.
choice Token
    Literal with c as a Char
    Any
    ZeroOrMore
    RecursivePrefix
    RecursiveSuffix
    RecursiveZeroOrMore
    Class with negated as a Bool and ranges as a List of CharRange
    Alternates with branches as a List of List of Token

type CharRange
    field start as a Char
    field end as a Char

type GlobOptions
    field case_insensitive as a Bool

type Glob
    field opts as a GlobOptions
    field tokens as a List of Token

note WORKAROUND: a Rust method on &self becomes an operation taking the Glob as an ordinary read-only argument.
to required_ext of glob using memory
    given glob is a Glob
    given memory is an Allocator
    produces a maybe Text
    fails with OutOfMemory
    uses memory
    note WORKAROUND: Rust aborts when allocation fails, so the original has no failure. Scribe makes allocation visible, so the Vec and String building adds `uses memory` and OutOfMemory.

    let opts be opts of glob
    if case_insensitive of opts
        give back nothing
    note We don't care at all about the beginning of this pattern. All we
    note need to check for is if it ends with a literal of the form `.ext`.
    note built in reverse
    var ext starts at []
    let tokens be tokens of glob
    note WORKAROUND: the doc has no reverse iteration, so `.iter().rev()` becomes an index loop counting from the end.
    for each k from 0 until count of tokens
        let t be item (count of tokens - 1 - k) of tokens
        note WORKAROUND: Rust matches the literal pattern Token::Literal('/') before Token::Literal(c). `when` lines bind payloads but cannot test a payload against a value, so the '/' case is an if inside the Literal branch.
        note UNCLEAR: whether `choose` needs every variant listed or whether there is a catch-all `when` line. The doc shows none, so every other variant is listed by name.
        choose t
            when Literal with c
                if c is "/"
                    give back nothing
                note GAP: no operation to append to a growable list is in the vocabulary table. `append value to list` appears only in example 9 and is used here.
                append c to ext
                if c is "."
                    stop
            when Any
                give back nothing
            when ZeroOrMore
                give back nothing
            when RecursivePrefix
                give back nothing
            when RecursiveSuffix
                give back nothing
            when RecursiveZeroOrMore
                give back nothing
            when Class with negated and ranges
                give back nothing
            when Alternates with branches
                give back nothing
    note WORKAROUND: Rust compares ext.last() with Some(&'.'), which also covers the empty case. Scribe needs the empty check written out.
    if count of ext is 0
        give back nothing
    if item (count of ext - 1) of ext is not "."
        give back nothing
    note GAP: building Text from a list of characters (ext.reverse() then collect) has no form in the doc. `text_from` is a guessed operation, and the reversal is a comprehension over indices.
    let ordered be item (count of ext - 1 - k) of ext for each k from 0 until count of ext
    give back some try text_from ordered using memory

to text_from chars using memory
    given chars is a List of Char
    given memory is an Allocator
    produces Text
    fails with OutOfMemory
    uses memory
